/// Lifecycle of a commercial sale document (RAKHAL-339, Sales — `FINANCE_V2_DESIGN.md`
/// §4.3, §5.1). Deliberately **separate from payment status** (UNPAID/PARTIALLY_PAID/
/// PAID/OVERDUE lives on `Receivable`, RAKHAL-340) — a `Sale` can be fully PAID while
/// still CONFIRMED, and a DRAFT sale has no payment status at all yet.
enum SaleStatus {
  /// Being built, not yet committed — no stock/ledger side effects.
  DRAFT
  /// Committed — the sale-type use case (RAKHAL-342/345/346/347) has run its
  /// atomic stock-decrement + receivable + journal posting.
  CONFIRMED
  /// Voided before any money moved.
  CANCELLED
  /// Fully reversed after money moved (a reversing use case, not built by this
  /// ticket — RD-058-adjacent follow-on work).
  REFUNDED
  /// Part of the sale reversed.
  PARTIALLY_REFUNDED
}

/// Which typed detail table a `SaleLine` carries (RAKHAL-339). Exactly one of
/// `MilkSaleLine`/`AnimalSaleLine`/`InventorySaleLine`/`ManureSaleLine` exists per
/// `SaleLine`, matched to this discriminator — enforced in `SaleService`, not the DB
/// (Prisma has no first-class "exactly one of N optional 1:1s" constraint).
enum SaleLineType {
  MILK
  ANIMAL
  INVENTORY
  MANURE
}
